# Beyond the Stars - DRAFT showcase script (docs/recording.md). About 4 minutes at 1920x1080, 30 fps.
#
# Every rig is built by script in a fresh creative superflat world; the captions say so. What runs on its own after
# that runs on its own: nothing is staged with commands. Time-lapses keep the game at its real rate and only thin out
# the frames (the tag says by how much, and the clock how much real time has passed).
#
# Sites: Rig C, the AE2 Eye (x 2400); Rig B, the Kerr on AE2 (x 1700); the Eye tier build (x 3600); the Kerr tiers
# (x 5000 / 5130); the build-logic Eye (x 3200); the plant tiers (x 6000 ...).
# TODO scenes are marked; they wait for content that is not on this branch.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- setup (never recorded)
build eyeae
build kerr
time day
command /btsquests install
# the Eye whose bands grow tier by tier (tier 1 by the dev kit, the rest by the projector in the tier scenes)
kit eye 1 3600,5,4000 name tiers
# the two Kerr tiers side by side
kit kerr t1 5000,36,4000 name kt1
kit kerr t2 5130,36,4000 name kt2
# the plant foundation at silo tiers 1-5 (/btsbuild console form), 60 blocks apart
command /btsbuild t1 6000 5 4000 north
command /btsbuild t2 6060 5 4000 north
command /btsbuild t3 6120 5 4000 north
command /btsbuild t4 6180 5 4000 north
command /btsbuild t5 6240 5 4000 north

# ================================================================ 1. title
scene title
  card 4 Beyond the Stars | Stars, black holes and the machines that run them | a GregTech: New Horizons 2.9 addon - recorded in game

# ================================================================ 2. the AE2 Eye rig
scene ae-intro
  caption An Eye of Harmony, tier 1, run by one AE2 network and nothing else: no hand on it, no GT covers, no redstone wiring. Built by script in a fresh creative world.
  orbit aeeye+0,-10,0 radius 100 height 32 from -55 to 35 seconds 10

scene ae-core
  caption The main ME network (orange) in front of the Eye: it stocks the Eye's gas and ignition charges and takes its products.
  goto ae.core+-3,7,-13 look ae.core+-3,0,1
  label ae.tankhe side left | Gas supply: endless test tanks behind read-only fluid storage buses, standing in for your Helium and Hydrogen production (set up by script)
  label ae.drive side up | ME drive: the ignition charges, and room for the star's products
  hold 4
  label clear
  label ae.core side left | ME controller (creative energy)
  label ae.emitter side right | Level emitter: its lamp is lit while a Stellar Ignition Charge is in stock
  hold 3

scene ae-trimnet
  caption The trims get their own small network (light blue; cables of different colours never join). On the main one, the Eye's stocking hatch would pull every litre into the Eye's buffers and leave the trim buses dry.
  goto ae.trimcore+2,7,-12 look ae.trimcore+2,0,1
  label ae.trimcore side left | Trim network: its own ME controller
  label ae.trimtank side right | and its own gas supply (test tanks, set up by script)
  hold 6

scene ae-trunk
  caption Along the ground trunk: what the network shows the Eye, and where the Eye's products go.
  label ae.stockbus side up | ME stocking input bus: shows the Eye an ignition charge
  label ae.outhatch side up | ME output hatch and bus: the star's products go straight into the network
  label ae.stockhatch side up | ME stocking input hatch: Helium and Hydrogen, drained into the Eye's buffers every second
  goto 2366,11,3982 look 2366,4,4003
  dolly 2366,11,3982 2434,11,3982 seconds 9 ease inout

scene ae-riser
  caption Two dense-cable risers carry the trim network 40 blocks up to the trim stations on the Eye's band.
  dolly 2440,8,3986 2440,46,3998 look ae.trimhe seconds 6

scene ae-trim
  caption A trim station. The Directive Hatch reads the star's field every second; while it wants Helium its bit is on, one redstone dust carries it onto the bus block, and the bus pushes Helium into the Field hatch.
  goto ae.trimhe.cam look ae.trimhe+0,0.5,0
  label ae.dirhe side up | Directive Hatch, Trims, Bit 1: on while the pressure is too high
  label ae.trimhe side left | AE2 fluid export bus (Helium) with a redstone card: runs only while the bit is on
  label ae.lamphe side right | Lamp on the same line: lit = Helium trim open
  label ae.fieldhe side down | A small (LV) Field hatch, so the bus cannot stockpile trim
  hold 7
  caption The Hydrogen station on the far side does the same on Bit 2, when the pressure is too low.
  hold 2

scene ae-light
  caption Now the gas supply opens and the charge cell goes into the drive (set up by script). From here nothing touches the Eye: it fills its buffers, takes a charge and lights its star by itself.
  goto aeeye+0,-14,-88 look aeeye+0,-6,0
  aecells
  timelapse 30 speed 10 until aelit tail 5 clock

scene ae-burn
  caption Sol is burning. The trim buses switch on and off to hold the field; the products flow into the ME network.
  orbit aeeye+0,-8,0 radius 80 height 20 from 30 to -30 seconds 12 speed 20 clock

# ================================================================ 3. the Eye's controller screen
scene eye-gui
  caption The Eye's controller screen: the star's state, the field gauges, stability and yield, the last event.
  goto aeeyectrl+0,0.2,-3.5 look aeeyectrl
  gui aeeyectrl
  hold 6
  close

# ================================================================ 4. Eye tiers
scene eye-t1
  caption Eye tiers. Tier 1, the core (19,616 blocks): plinth, band and field generators. It burns Sol, which makes Raw Star Matter.
  fov 75
  goto tiers.c+-125,42,-125 look tiers.c+0,-8,0
  hold 5

scene eye-t2
  caption Tier 2 adds the beam band. Its star is Sirius A (Excited Stellar Plasma). To get there: a Stellar Mass Core and the Mass Infusion transition.
  hologram tiers survival tier 2 budget 4 every 1 tail 2 max 25

scene eye-t3
  caption Tier 3 adds the jet crescent. Its star is Arcturus (Raw Hyperdense Stellar Plasma). To get there: a Shell-Burning Core and the Shell Ignition.
  hologram tiers survival tier 3 budget 4 every 1 tail 2 max 25

scene eye-t4
  caption Tier 4 adds the spiral arms. Its star is a neutron star (White Dwarf Matter). To get there: a Galactic Upgrade Core and the Core Collapse.
  hologram tiers survival tier 4 budget 5 every 1 tail 2 max 25

scene eye-t5
  caption Tier 5 adds the second arms. Its star is Sirius B (Black Dwarf Matter). To get there: a Subspace Cooling Core and the First Cooling.
  hologram tiers survival tier 5 budget 5 every 1 tail 2 max 25

scene eye-t6
  caption Tier 6 adds the galactic rim and four more stellar sockets. Its star is the magnetar (Magnetar Matter): a Magnetar Seed Core and the Magnetar Merger.
  hologram tiers survival tier 6 budget 6 every 1 tail 1 max 30
  caption Every tier also needs its Spacetime Compression generators, and each tier above a recipe's own doubles that recipe's parallel.
  orbit tiers.c+0,-8,0 radius 170 height 50 from -45 to 45 seconds 9
  fov 70

# ================================================================ 5. the Kerr
scene kerr-rig
  caption The Kerr Ergosphere Engine, tier 1, on AE2: one Directive Hatch per job, each switching an export bus on demand.
  goto k.core+0,7,-22 look k.core+0,-2,8
  label k.boltdir side up | Directive Hatch, Hole Bit 3: the bolt stock runs short
  label k.boltbus side right | Export bus (redstone card): SpaceTime bolts into the bolt bus
  label k.seedbus side left | Export bus: a Black Hole Seed while the hole is closed (Bit 1)
  label k.core side down | ME controller, drive and interface
  hold 7

scene kerr-run
  caption The cell of bolts and seeds goes into the drive (set up by script). The network seeds the hole, then feeds it bolts as it climbs to its setpoint.
  goto kerr+60,18,-70 look kerr
  cell
  orbit kerr radius 90 height 22 from -40 to 40 seconds 14 speed 30 clock

scene kerr-gui
  caption The Kerr's controller screen: the hole's mass against its setpoint, the bolt stock and the modules.
  goto keectrl+0,0.2,-3.5 look keectrl
  gui keectrl
  hold 6
  close

scene kerr-tiers
  caption Kerr tiers side by side (built by the dev kit). Tier 1: setpoint 2 to 64 solar masses. Tier 2, with the Kerr Density Upgrade, a heavier shell: setpoint up to 512, and the Compressor Module gains Kerr Densification (a hole of 128 or more).
  label kt1.c side up | Tier 1
  label kt2.c side up | Tier 2
  goto 4985,62,3850 look 4985,30,4040
  dolly 4985,62,3850 5145,62,3850 seconds 10

# ================================================================ 6. how a player builds one
scene build-hints
  caption How a player builds one. Place the controller and use a Hologram Projector on it: the whole structure appears as hints.
  place bts.eyeOfHarmony 3200,5,4000 facing north name build1
  goto build1+-70,45,-60 look build1+0,10,40
  hologram build1 hints
  hold 4

scene build-survival
  caption Sneak-use it in survival and it places the blocks from your inventory, in this order, a batch per use (items supplied by script).
  hologram build1 survival tier 1 budget 4 every 1 tail 1 max 40

scene build-form
  caption With the hatches fitted (here by the dev kit), the controller checks the structure and forms: Eye of Harmony T1.
  kit eye 1 build1
  goto build1+0,0.2,-3.5 look build1
  gui build1
  hold 5
  close

scene build-nei
  caption NEI shows every multiblock: the structure preview, with its tier and layer sliders, and the blocks it takes.
  nei usage bts.eyeOfHarmony tab multiblock
  hold 6
  close

scene build-recipe
  caption And how the controller itself is made.
  nei recipe bts.eyeOfHarmony
  hold 5
  close

# ================================================================ 7. other multis of ours on this branch
scene plant-tiers
  caption The Nuclear Plant Foundation's silo tiers 1 to 5, raised by its dev command: bigger silo, more fuel pillars, heavier walls, a taller plant.
  goto 5990,70,3920 look 5990,20,4040
  dolly 5990,70,3920 6250,70,3920 seconds 12

scene todo-later
  # TODO: master content. The Bose-Einstein condensate chain is recipes only on this branch, and the Homogeny and
  # Reality machines do not exist here; film them on master once merged.
  card 4 Coming next | the Bose-Einstein Condensate chain, the Homogeny and the Reality machines | (not on this build yet)

# ================================================================ 8. the quest book
scene questbook
  caption The quest book: the addon's chapter leads a player from the first plant to the endgame, one step at a time.
  questbook chapter
  hold 5
  close
  caption Each quest says what to build, what done looks like, and pays the next step's tool.
  questbook quest 48000
  hold 5
  close

# ================================================================ 9. end
scene end
  card 4 Beyond the Stars | Draft showcase - recorded in a GTNH 2.9 dev client | more soon
